<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40519" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-calfacĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕcălĕfacĭo</span></b> ),
			fēci, 3, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make warm</i> (<i>again</i>), <i>to warm</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-class. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calidumque priori Caede recalfecit consorti
					sanguine telum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 443</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. F. 4, 698</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. A. 2,
				214</span></i>.—<i>Pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rursus recalfiunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 271</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Acut. 2, 10,
			63</span></i>.—Full form: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">statim recalefacto corpore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 2, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tepidam recalface mentem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 2, 445</span></i>
			.</div>
